# Benchmark build artifacts — regenerated by crisp-compile / crisp-hoist-cuda on every run.
# Do not check these in.

# Hoist byproducts (metadata + per-kernel generated harnesses).
*.metacrisp
*_CUDA.cu

# Compiled kernels (.ptx / .spv) are regenerable too — but a few are committed as fallbacks
# for machines where crisp-compile is absent, so they are re-included by exception below:
#   run.py                 ships crisp/matmul.ptx + crisp/matmul_async.ptx to a Linux CUDA pod
#   bench-intel-driver.py  ships the .spv into the oneAPI Docker container
# Everything else (matmul_async_block.ptx, matmul_pipelined.ptx, …) is a throwaway artifact.
*.ptx
*.spv
!matmul/crisp/matmul.ptx
!matmul/crisp/matmul_async.ptx
!matmul/crisp/matmul_bmg.spv
!matmul/crisp/matmul_bmg_async.spv
!reduction/crisp/sum-reduce.spv
